WEBVTT

00:11.700 --> 00:15.560
A lot of things happened, 
but our gold smuggling operation was a success.

00:15.560 --> 00:18.620
We were able to secure my future as a merchant,

00:18.620 --> 00:21.540
as well as open the path 
of a tailor to Ms. Nora.

00:24.080 --> 00:26.790
Let's drink and eat our fill today.

00:27.230 --> 00:29.750
Now, cheers to a bright future ahead!

00:33.470 --> 00:37.690
Spice and Wolf

00:37.690 --> 00:38.810
Spice and Wolf

00:38.810 --> 00:44.150
Spice and Wolf

02:02.350 --> 02:06.350
<b>Episode 13
Supper of Three and Afternoon of Two</b>

02:02.390 --> 02:04.470
What? Is that what happened?

02:03.740 --> 02:04.470
Yes!

02:04.730 --> 02:06.480
That was truly impressive.

02:06.920 --> 02:07.850
Not at all!

02:07.850 --> 02:09.550
As expected of you, Ms. Nora.

02:09.550 --> 02:13.230
It was only because the sheep 
were all very obedient.

02:13.230 --> 02:17.820
Don't be modest. It's because you are 
a really skilled shepherd.

02:17.820 --> 02:19.530
That's not true...

02:20.260 --> 02:21.870
Oh, it's here.

02:21.870 --> 02:23.290
It looks delicious.

02:23.290 --> 02:24.240
Let's cut into it.

02:30.930 --> 02:31.580
Here.

02:31.580 --> 02:33.000
Thank you very much.

02:33.000 --> 02:34.790
You're welcome.

02:34.790 --> 02:36.140
Do you want some, too?

02:39.020 --> 02:40.520
Let me know if you want some.

02:41.350 --> 02:45.180
Even so, I didn't know 
sheep could find rock salt.

02:45.180 --> 02:48.670
For some reason, they really love salty things.

02:48.670 --> 02:54.020
For instance, if you rub some salt onto a rock, 
they'll stay there and lick it forever.

02:57.000 --> 03:05.240
Come to think of it, I once heard that 
a faraway town used sheep as a torture method.

03:05.240 --> 03:08.380
I thought such a thing would be impossible.

03:08.380 --> 03:09.870
Using sheep?

03:09.870 --> 03:13.640
Yes, I've forgotten the name of the town,

03:13.640 --> 03:18.220
but it's said that they have 
sheep lick the prisoner's feet.

03:18.220 --> 03:18.670
Huh?

03:18.670 --> 03:19.980
The sheep?

03:26.150 --> 03:30.940
Yes. They have the sheep lick the person's 
feet by slathering salt on them.

03:30.940 --> 03:34.490
At first, it only feels ticklish, 
but the sheep don't stop,

03:34.490 --> 03:36.730
and they end up laughing so much it's painful.

03:36.730 --> 03:38.000
Oh, my!

03:38.000 --> 03:41.630
Have your sheep ever licked 
your hands or fingers before?

03:41.630 --> 03:44.980
It's true that my sheep have gathered around me

03:44.980 --> 03:49.370
before trying to lick my hands 
after I've eaten some dried meat.

03:49.370 --> 03:53.310
In comparison, it seems that the knight 
at your side is quite obedient.

03:56.250 --> 04:03.310
Hmm, well, there are times when Enek tries 
a little too hard or gets a little stubborn.

04:12.020 --> 04:16.860
If that's the case, you must truly be 
a skilled shepherd to guide all of them.

04:16.860 --> 04:19.020
Well, that's...

04:21.690 --> 04:24.590
By the way, Ms. Nora, are you planning...

04:27.950 --> 04:30.320
What's the matter? Are you already drunk?

04:32.840 --> 04:34.550
Your face looks pale!

04:34.550 --> 04:38.220
It's nothing, I'm just...

04:40.110 --> 04:40.840
Holo!

04:40.840 --> 04:44.460
Holo! Hey! Get a hold of yourself! Holo!

04:46.030 --> 04:50.470
<i>For hundreds of years, 
I have lived alone in those wheat fields.</i>

04:50.830 --> 04:54.770
<i>They were peaceful days.</i>

04:54.770 --> 04:56.960
<i>One could not tell the difference 
between yesterday and today,</i>

04:56.960 --> 04:59.050
<i>much less tomorrow or the day after that.</i>

04:59.320 --> 05:05.070
<i>I would only be reminded 
of the concept of time on festival days.</i>

05:05.420 --> 05:10.400
<i>In a year, there would be 
one harvest festival, two planting festivals,</i>

05:10.400 --> 05:13.700
<i>a festival to pray that 
there wouldn't be frost,</i>

05:13.700 --> 05:16.040
<i>a festival to pray for rain,</i>

05:16.360 --> 05:19.310
<i>and a festival to pray for calm winds.</i>

05:21.170 --> 05:24.760
<i>In comparison, the days of my travel 
are filled with so many new things</i>

05:24.760 --> 05:27.000
<i>that I feel as if I were born again.</i>

05:27.420 --> 05:29.710
<i>The days I have experienced 
since meeting my traveling companion</i>

05:29.710 --> 05:32.350
<i>are already comparable to 
hundreds of years worth of my life.</i>

05:33.180 --> 05:37.110
<i>Even in a single day, the morning and evening 
are completely different experiences.</i>

05:37.390 --> 05:42.140
<i>We may argue vigorously in the morning, 
but reconcile in the afternoon,</i>

05:42.140 --> 05:45.230
<i>having him take breadcrumbs 
off my face while teasing him,</i>

05:45.230 --> 05:48.080
<i>only to fight with him once again 
over the food at supper,</i>

05:48.080 --> 05:50.700
<i>then quietly talk about the plans 
of tomorrow at night.</i>

05:52.190 --> 05:56.540
<i>I have traveled and lived with 
other humans in the past.</i>

05:56.540 --> 05:58.730
<i>I have unforgettable memories as well.</i>

06:00.200 --> 06:03.670
<i>However, there is never 
a chance to get lost in them.</i>

06:04.550 --> 06:08.800
<i>I am busy wondering what my companion was 
doing the day before, how he was this morning,</i>

06:08.800 --> 06:11.930
<i>and what he may be scheming 
at this very moment.</i>

06:12.420 --> 06:18.360
<i>I only had time to recall my birthplace 
with sad nostalgia when I first met him.</i>

06:18.810 --> 06:24.320
<i>With days so full of excitement that it makes 
me dizzy, I have no time to feel such sadness.</i>

06:24.750 --> 06:26.690
<i>It would be a lie to say I am not having fun.</i>

06:27.100 --> 06:31.320
<i>In fact, I am having 
so much fun that I feel uneasy.</i>

06:39.470 --> 06:40.970
<i>Where am I?</i>

06:49.330 --> 06:50.880
<i>What a blunder.</i>

06:53.270 --> 06:54.940
<i>I wonder why.</i>

06:55.410 --> 06:59.420
<i>I get angry when it is not to my liking, 
laugh because it is funny,</i>

06:59.770 --> 07:03.060
<i>and end up exposing my weak side...</i>

07:03.060 --> 07:06.020
No, this is all the fault of that man!

07:06.360 --> 07:10.740
<i>We were able to overcome this ordeal 
thanks to this Wise Wolf!</i>

07:10.740 --> 07:16.050
<i>What is so good about the meager 
form of that shepherd?</i>

07:16.050 --> 07:18.150
<i>Is it her blonde hair?</i>

07:18.790 --> 07:21.740
<i>Where is that man right now?</i>

07:21.740 --> 07:27.170
<i>To think he is not at my side in my time 
of need. He is truly a failure as a male...</i>

07:51.290 --> 07:53.640
Why didn't you tell me 
you weren't feeling well?

07:55.290 --> 07:56.410
You're not a child.

07:56.820 --> 07:59.700
Don't tell me you didn't realize it 
until you fainted?

08:00.000 --> 08:01.810
I was really worried about you.

08:01.810 --> 08:04.700
What if this happened 
in the middle of traveling?

08:04.700 --> 08:07.380
Even a small incident can lead to one's death.

08:08.150 --> 08:09.300
I am sorry.

08:10.090 --> 08:12.420
Well, I'm just glad that you're okay.

08:12.770 --> 08:15.690
It's not a cold or sickness, is it?

08:17.290 --> 08:19.420
I think my exhaustion 
has merely caught up to me.

08:19.420 --> 08:21.020
As I thought.

08:21.020 --> 08:23.770
I'm pretty knowledgeable about sicknesses.

08:24.280 --> 08:25.230
It's just that...

08:25.230 --> 08:29.980
I thought maybe it was from 
eating onion or something.

08:29.980 --> 08:32.780
I am not a dog!

08:32.780 --> 08:35.050
Yeah, you're a Wise Wolf.

08:35.050 --> 08:38.820
However, I regret wasting the wine 
and sumptuous meal.

08:39.400 --> 08:42.930
I'm a merchant. And I am no fool.

08:42.930 --> 08:45.000
I wrapped up all the leftovers 
and brought them back with us.

08:45.960 --> 08:47.710
Is what I'd like to say, but...

08:57.340 --> 08:59.340
As I thought, you have a fever.

08:59.340 --> 09:01.390
You must have been really tired.

09:01.390 --> 09:02.970
It is all your fault.

09:02.970 --> 09:04.140
Huh? Me?

09:04.140 --> 09:09.060
Your fingers are hard and 
similar to the nose of a wolf.

09:10.390 --> 09:14.970
Rubbing your nose on me, in human terms...

09:16.180 --> 09:17.250
I cannot say it out loud.

09:17.250 --> 09:18.660
What nonsense is that?

09:18.660 --> 09:21.360
Enough! Leave me alone!

09:21.360 --> 09:23.670
Well, you'll need to stay away 
from meat for a while.

09:26.890 --> 09:30.350
In exchange, I'll make some food that is 
easy to eat for the sick tomorrow.

09:30.350 --> 09:32.130
Rest well and recover your strength.

09:32.130 --> 09:34.760
I feel like there will be a heavy price 
to pay when you act with kindness.

09:34.760 --> 09:36.800
I should be the one saying that.

09:53.260 --> 09:56.030
Where has he gone and what is he doing?

09:56.030 --> 10:00.270
In Yoitsu, taking care of the sick means 
grooming the other's fur with their tongue

10:00.270 --> 10:01.950
and huddling close to give them warmth.

10:02.200 --> 10:04.840
I cannot believe he is not by 
my side when I open my eyes!

10:10.280 --> 10:11.610
How are you feeling?

10:11.610 --> 10:13.130
I cannot sit up.

10:13.700 --> 10:15.400
You're probably lying.

10:16.710 --> 10:19.310
Well, then. I'll have some 
porridge made for you.

10:19.310 --> 10:22.510
My throat is parched. Is that water?

10:22.510 --> 10:26.530
Oh. No, you had a fever yesterday, didn't you?

10:26.530 --> 10:28.140
That's why I brought some apple wine.

10:31.610 --> 10:32.720
What's the matter?

10:32.720 --> 10:34.720
The covers are too heavy.

10:37.100 --> 10:37.990
How's that?

10:38.470 --> 10:39.760
My apologies.

10:54.940 --> 10:56.000
What's the matter?

10:56.000 --> 10:57.540
The flavor...

10:57.540 --> 10:59.380
Oh, I diluted it.

10:59.380 --> 11:04.110
This is much too diluted! 
I thought something was wrong with my nose!

11:04.110 --> 11:05.760
You had a fever, didn't you?

11:05.760 --> 11:07.720
That's why you get diluted apple wine.

11:07.720 --> 11:09.390
Why is that the case?

11:09.390 --> 11:13.190
Oh, I see. You don't know 
about stuff like this.

11:13.850 --> 11:15.940
I ran to a trading house when you fainted

11:15.940 --> 11:19.520
and read through translated 
medical books in a panic.

11:20.070 --> 11:22.570
And what was written in those texts?

11:22.570 --> 11:26.360
Sickness is when the balance 
of a person's body crumbles.

11:26.360 --> 11:28.910
Things like exhaustion or miasma can cause it.

11:28.910 --> 11:32.180
The body can also be affected 
by the alignment of the stars.

11:32.180 --> 11:35.210
You can heal the sick 
by restoring the patient's balance.

11:35.640 --> 11:39.090
To do that, you must make use 
of the four temperaments.

11:39.090 --> 11:41.010
Four temperaments?

11:41.330 --> 11:47.890
Yeah, the four temperaments of the human 
body are warm, cold, dry, and moist.

11:47.890 --> 11:50.640
You can balance those temperaments 
with the food you eat.

11:50.970 --> 11:54.500
That's because food can also be 
categorized into hot foods,

11:54.500 --> 11:58.170
cold foods, dry foods, and moist foods.

11:58.610 --> 12:02.740
You currently have a fever, so cold foods 
like apples are perfect for you.

12:02.740 --> 12:07.030
If that is the case, 
I would rather eat fresh apples.

12:07.030 --> 12:09.130
That's not good enough.

12:09.130 --> 12:10.520
While apples are considered a cold food,

12:10.520 --> 12:13.300
they're also medically 
categorized as a dry food.

12:13.300 --> 12:16.960
Sick people are often dry, 
so they have to be kept moist.

12:18.280 --> 12:20.740
That's why it had to be a drink.

12:20.740 --> 12:23.020
It's just that strong alcohol 
is considered hot,

12:23.020 --> 12:25.220
so I had to dilute it to keep it cold.

12:26.530 --> 12:32.560
So, that is why I am drinking this 
terrible tasting water with a hint of color.

12:32.560 --> 12:36.990
So? What kind of food will you have me eat?

12:36.990 --> 12:42.030
Well, since you had an exhaustion fever, 
we need to cool you down first.

12:42.030 --> 12:45.880
Your body should also be dry, 
so we'll have to replenish your moisture.

12:47.160 --> 12:49.520
Don't you get thirsty after running?

12:49.520 --> 12:52.000
However, moist things will cool down the body

12:52.000 --> 12:54.480
and if it gets too cold 
people will become melancholic.

12:54.480 --> 12:57.080
That's why we have to warm you up, too.

12:57.080 --> 12:58.100
Putting that into consideration...

12:58.570 --> 13:03.020
Putting that into consideration, 
some wheat grains simmered in sheep milk

13:03.020 --> 13:06.590
with slices of apples and cheese should work.

13:08.740 --> 13:10.760
The reason, starting with the apples...

13:11.260 --> 13:14.660
Yes, that is good. That is what I wish to eat.

13:14.660 --> 13:17.150
No, if I do not eat it, 
I will collapse once again.

13:17.150 --> 13:20.480
Look. My face is so pale.

13:20.900 --> 13:23.560
Come, now, bring it here quickly!

13:23.560 --> 13:26.910
You're actually all better, aren't you?

13:27.560 --> 13:29.890
I feel dizzy...

13:29.890 --> 13:31.780
H-Hey! Get a hold of yourself!

13:32.810 --> 13:34.370
Please hurry.

13:37.780 --> 13:38.810
Goodness...

13:39.250 --> 13:41.680
So, you don't want any more apple wine?

13:42.250 --> 13:43.840
Well, this is fine as it is, as well.

13:45.260 --> 13:46.970
Make sure the porridge portion is large.

13:47.280 --> 13:49.050
Sure. Sure.

14:01.430 --> 14:04.030
<i>Sometimes, I dream.</i>

14:04.320 --> 14:08.060
<i>I dream of my birthplace, 
and I dream of the wheat fields.</i>

14:08.670 --> 14:10.280
<i>While they are both nostalgic dreams,</i>

14:10.280 --> 14:14.340
<i>there is an overwhelming feeling 
of repulsion along with them.</i>

14:14.930 --> 14:17.290
<i>As an existence that stands above others,</i>

14:17.290 --> 14:21.530
<i>they were both times that I had to 
accept and fulfill my responsibilities.</i>

14:22.630 --> 14:28.550
<i>Neither was I asked, nor did I ask for it, 
but it was a duty that someone must do.</i>

14:28.550 --> 14:35.060
<i>Before I realized it, the heavy, heavy shackle 
had already dug itself into my neck.</i>

14:36.370 --> 14:38.490
<i>They depend on me because I am powerful,</i>

14:38.490 --> 14:42.690
<i>they revere me because of my immense size, 
and they honor me because I am useful.</i>

14:43.050 --> 14:46.430
<i>I did not ask for their worship,</i>

14:46.430 --> 14:50.820
<i>but I could not abandon them 
and let myself be imprisoned.</i>

14:51.800 --> 14:55.940
<i>Neither did I ask for the responsibility 
nor was asked to take it,</i>

14:56.360 --> 14:58.430
<i>yet hundreds of years passed by.</i>

14:59.790 --> 15:02.540
<i>I am used to sniffing the aroma 
of delicious food.</i>

15:02.540 --> 15:05.900
<i>And yet, until now, I had never seen a person</i>

15:05.900 --> 15:11.310
<i>who would give me such a friendly smile 
when my nose twitched at the smell of food.</i>

15:11.310 --> 15:17.880
<i>Though, that human is an impudent one 
that does not know his place.</i>

15:22.500 --> 15:23.610
Can you prop yourself up?

15:28.260 --> 15:29.690
Goodness...

15:29.690 --> 15:33.580
You better take really good care 
of me if I ever get sick.

15:33.580 --> 15:35.870
As long as the traditions 
of Yoitsu are acceptable.

15:35.870 --> 15:37.010
What's that supposed to mean?

15:37.010 --> 15:40.140
Do not worry. 
I have an exceptionally good nose.

15:40.140 --> 15:43.610
I will notice before you get to this point 
and do something about it.

15:44.520 --> 15:46.840
Well, it's my fault for not noticing sooner.

15:47.700 --> 15:50.740
But I hope you say something 
to me first, next time.

15:51.260 --> 15:55.220
I'm, well, pretty dense 
about this kind of thing.

15:56.070 --> 15:57.640
That is true.

15:57.940 --> 16:00.490
I expect you would be slow 
to notice a certain sickness

16:00.490 --> 16:02.650
that even doctors cannot heal, as well.

16:02.650 --> 16:03.140
Huh?

16:03.140 --> 16:04.910
It is nothing.

16:04.910 --> 16:06.490
More importantly, food.

16:06.490 --> 16:08.730
Goodness, are you some kind of princess?

16:25.660 --> 16:28.550
Will you use the spoon and feed me?

16:30.880 --> 16:31.920
Here you go.

16:41.740 --> 16:44.920
It would be more delicious with more apples.

16:44.920 --> 16:48.620
Maybe. Cold apples might make you 
a little more melancholic.

16:48.980 --> 16:50.340
Are you...

16:51.400 --> 16:54.070
Are you saying I am too merry?

16:54.070 --> 16:57.260
I'm just saying it wouldn't hurt 
to become a little quieter.

17:03.630 --> 17:06.950
Well, I'm a little relieved 
seeing you eat this much.

17:06.950 --> 17:09.500
I'm sure you'll get better in a day or two.

17:09.500 --> 17:11.420
Well, there's no rush.

17:11.420 --> 17:14.630
We'll be traveling on my cart 
for a while after we leave town.

17:14.630 --> 17:16.340
You can take your time to recover.

17:19.060 --> 17:20.560
But, you know...

17:21.790 --> 17:27.400
The inn is, well, too quiet...

17:29.530 --> 17:32.570
True. It's noisy when we travel by cart.

17:33.330 --> 17:35.900
I don't have anything to do today.

17:36.530 --> 17:41.280
And, I still need to get advice on what 
a certain big eater should eat this evening.

17:41.680 --> 17:45.010
So, do you have a rough idea 
of what you'd like to eat?

17:45.010 --> 17:47.370
I won't be able to prepare the right 
ingredients after the market closes.

17:50.390 --> 17:55.840
You may look energetic, but that may not 
hold true on the inside. No heavy food.

17:57.400 --> 17:58.520
Even meat?

17:58.520 --> 18:01.870
No way. You can eat porridge 
or maybe bread soaked in soup...

18:03.570 --> 18:05.410
Then, I wish to eat the same thing.

18:05.410 --> 18:10.380
Sheep milk, was it? It was deliciously sweet 
and rich at the same time. I want that.

18:10.380 --> 18:11.950
Sheep milk, huh?

18:12.900 --> 18:14.320
Is there a problem?

18:14.680 --> 18:18.320
It spoils easily, so good sheep milk 
is really expensive after noon.

18:18.320 --> 18:20.400
You want it fresh, don't you?

18:20.400 --> 18:21.370
Of course.

18:21.370 --> 18:24.650
Well, I guess I'll have Nora 
go find some again.

18:24.650 --> 18:27.060
Since she's a shepherd, she has a good eye.

18:27.060 --> 18:28.490
Nora, you say?

18:30.600 --> 18:34.190
No, I just want to 
get some good milk for you...

18:34.190 --> 18:37.130
If you spend enough money, it doesn't 
matter if you have a good eye or not!

18:37.130 --> 18:40.730
Th-There's no reason not to hire a guide!

18:41.410 --> 18:42.220
However!

18:42.540 --> 18:45.810
However, why do you treat Nora 
like a sworn enemy?

18:46.600 --> 18:48.190
Wh-What did you say?

18:48.190 --> 18:53.230
W-Well, I don't know what happened 
between you and shepherds in the past.

18:53.520 --> 18:56.320
I also know that you don't like them 
because you're a wolf.

18:56.320 --> 18:59.990
But is there a reason to be so openly hostile?

18:59.990 --> 19:02.670
Nora may be a shepherd, 
but how do I say this...

19:02.670 --> 19:04.950
I mean, she has such a sweet disposition.

19:04.950 --> 19:07.030
There are always exceptions to everything.

19:10.010 --> 19:11.080
Hey.

19:11.080 --> 19:12.730
Wh-What?

19:12.730 --> 19:14.450
I am in the wrong.

19:14.450 --> 19:16.340
Is that so? Good to hear.

19:16.340 --> 19:19.560
However, one does not like or dislike 
something based on logic.

19:19.560 --> 19:20.990
I have told you this once before.

19:20.990 --> 19:25.100
I understand that. I don't think that 
everything can be explained clearly with reason.

19:25.500 --> 19:27.140
Then, I'm going to go return this.

19:27.140 --> 19:29.260
And, so...

19:29.260 --> 19:30.480
What is it now?

19:34.990 --> 19:38.530
Will you come right back after returning that?

19:39.020 --> 19:43.280
Yeah, of course. 
The inn is pretty quiet, after all.

19:44.470 --> 19:46.660
Okay, wait here obediently.

20:07.530 --> 20:08.230
Holo.

20:14.900 --> 20:16.940
Ms. Nora has come to visit you.

20:20.530 --> 20:22.490
How are you feeling?

20:23.610 --> 20:27.030
Well, it is just that my exhaustion 
has gotten to me.

20:27.440 --> 20:30.520
However, I was looking for someone to talk to.

20:30.520 --> 20:35.320
That is why I wish to ask you something 
that I was always curious about.

20:35.320 --> 20:37.210
Huh? A question for me?

20:37.770 --> 20:40.210
I'll gladly answer if I can.

20:41.590 --> 20:45.220
What is the greatest secret 
to guiding sheep well?

20:52.190 --> 20:54.810
Probably having a generous heart.

21:04.970 --> 21:06.160
I see.

21:08.150 --> 21:09.860
The wind is picking up.

21:13.370 --> 21:16.710
After all, sheep all think that they are smart.

23:14.080 --> 23:16.430
And that is the story.

23:16.430 --> 23:18.580
Really, do you not think him 
a troublesome sheep?

23:18.580 --> 23:22.600
Was the wolf able to handle 
the sheep well after that?

23:22.600 --> 23:24.790
Well, I wonder.

23:25.710 --> 23:28.210
The story doesn't end there, right?

23:28.210 --> 23:29.540
Of course not.

23:29.540 --> 23:30.810
Then, more!

23:32.460 --> 23:34.220
Tell me more about it!

23:35.610 --> 23:37.930
Hey, now. Do not rush me so.

23:38.950 --> 23:43.940
As the wolf continued her journey home, 
the place they both headed to next was...

23:44.980 --> 23:49.990
Episode 14

23:44.980 --> 23:49.990
New Town and Nostalgic Feeling

23:45.640 --> 23:49.350
Next Episode: New Town and Nostalgic Feeling
